 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Not exactly. It' called a century because it's one hundred miles, and horse riders do them usually. You can give yourself longer if you ride slower. Roughly ten hours, including stops. It depends how fast you ride and how long those stops are. It is. You' see lots of countryside and probably some nice villages too. Bring snacks and water, and don't rush. Start whichever one feels right. They're basically the same as you ride them. Lots of miles at nice pace at first gets you ready. There are online training plans if you want follow one.",
